      "value": "@{5ac4fd763f8d523278a414f7|full_name}:  how exactly do you determine who is doing useful stuff and who isn't? It sucks you can't pay for things online but in reality the actions of the minority affect the majority. It is why laws get put in place. It is why taxes are created. It sucks but to prevent the minority from affecting everyone people have to be harsh. Which is why article 13 is going to ruin stuff like twitch because if one person breaks copyright then it affects the platform. The same applies here. For things to get better there needs to be proper consequences for bad behaviour. Losing money after getting their account banned is one way. Again i can understand that it would suck for you being unable to pay but you could possibly talk to someone in vrchat devs and support if that is the case assuming it is actually implimented",
