  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-12-03T23:11:22.243Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Here's the deal. Right now VRChat has such bad issues with hackers, crashers, etc because there's really no consequence to it. \n\nNow imagine this. The GAME is still free to play. You can go to any world, grab any avatar in those worlds, BUT, now to upload your own content to the game (Worlds, avatars, etc.) You have to pay a one time small fee, say $5.00 and on that account you can now upload avatars and worlds freely as you can now. Now suddenly, think about how much this could fix if implemented correctly.\n\nSuddenly the game has a steady flow of income allowing for the dev team to pay for more people to work on the game, maybe pay the current devs more, buy more or better servers, etc. Along with this now there is a consequence to having your account banned. You get banned, you lose those permission and therefore lose money, eliminating the thought that you can go in the game and just ban evade. \n\nYou could possibly even catch ban evading easier when you see a payment method (certain card, steam account payment maybe, or paypal account, etc.) registered from one banned account pop up on another. \n\nThis realistically won't get rid of hackers, crashers, etc, entirely, but it sure would discourage many. Plus with more money coming in that can also go towards future upgrades of security. \n\nI've talked with a lot of people in game about this and not a single person has said they would mind paying one time to have the permissions to upload avatars and worlds if it would fix the current game issues. I highly suggest this option be taken into consideration.",
